{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets","id":308507,"title":"When can a Scion Dodge Bullets?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-10T14:23:46-08:00","id":308507,"title":"When can a Scion Dodge Bullets?","content":"Rules question:<br /> I know that, given a stunt, Whirlwind Shield will allow a Scion to parry a bullet. Does a resource exist to allow a Scion to dodge a bullet?<br /> <br /> Pretty sure that around God, Epic Dex allows a Scion to outrun a bullet. I feel like dodging ought to be buried in there somewhere, but darned if I can find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3712-quantumpants","name":"QuantumPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:19:38-08:00","id":308547,"title":"","content":"Scions can dodge bullets whenever they want. Whirlwind Shield is a terrible knack that implies rules that do not exist anywhere else.<br /> It's only useful if you don't have a single dot in Athletics, or you are a high strength character using knacks like Legendary Parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:07:37-08:00","id":308646,"title":"","content":"Scions can dodge bullets whenever the shooter fails to exceed their Dodge DV. So I guess a good resource for that is Dexterity, Athletics and Legend? And Epic Dex, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:55:50-08:00","id":309772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=308547#post308547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions can dodge bullets whenever they want. Whirlwind Shield is a terrible knack that implies rules that do not exist anywhere else.<br /> It's only useful if you don't have a single dot in Athletics, or you are a high strength character using knacks like Legendary Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is likely a leftover of the fact that they raided Aberrant and Exalted for their game play rules and weren't careful about checking when they dropped some mechanics.<br /> <br /> The game also, in different places, says that armor provides Agg soak equal to Lethal soak while all the character write ups suggest that worn armor does not provide Agg soak which further supported by the fact that are rules for allowing worn armor to provide Agg soak even when it doesn't normally.<br /> <br /> My group has something we say when we run across these pieces of....frustration:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Damn it, Scion!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T05:39:24-08:00","id":310074,"title":"","content":"No one can dodge bullets... you can move out from the line of sight, that's what you really dodge when you &quot;dodge a bullet&quot;. If there were a knack to dodge bullets, I would say knacks from Epic Wits. It's all about reflexes so probably something linked to Rabbit Reflexes. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T11:42:49-08:00","id":310415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=310074#post310074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one can dodge bullets... you can move out from the line of sight, that's what you really dodge when you &quot;dodge a bullet&quot;. If there were a knack to dodge bullets, I would say knacks from Epic Wits. It's all about reflexes so probably something linked to Rabbit Reflexes. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Im not sure why you would say that. Scions can definitely dodge bullets at legend 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T00:39:05-08:00","id":312037,"title":"","content":"Yeah, by Legend 2 or 3 it is possible to pull off legitimate dodging of gunfire.<br /> <br /> By Legend 5, it's practically Spider-Man reaction times where you can dodge individual bullets within a machine gun's spray....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T11:16:42-08:00","id":312446,"title":"","content":"Scions can, by default, dodge bullets. The combat chapter, page 192, specifically talks about defense in relationship with bullets. &quot;Bullets may not be parried without some special ability&quot;. That's stupid, but if the intent was bullets also being undodgeable without special abilities, then there'd be a note there as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T14:48:35-08:00","id":312565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=312446#post312446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions can, by default, dodge bullets. The combat chapter, page 192, specifically talks about defense in relationship with bullets. &quot;Bullets may not be parried without some special ability&quot;. That's stupid, but if the intent was bullets also being undodgeable without special abilities, then there'd be a note there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book references some attacks as being &quot;undodgeable&quot;, but not in regards to firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T15:00:28-08:00","id":312595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=312565#post312565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book references some attacks as being &quot;undodgeable&quot;, but not in regards to firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certain attacks can definitely be undodgeable by storyteller fiat. Usually some kind of AOE that is larger than your movement, and there is no meaningful cover nearby.<br /> Which is often rare, considering another member of the party might be viable cover. But there's usually at least one girl that has to take it on the chin.<br /> And there are a variety of boons that would be undodgeable as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 11-14-2014, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T20:29:18-08:00","id":313458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=309772#post309772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is likely a leftover of the fact that they raided Aberrant and Exalted for their game play rules and weren't careful about checking when they dropped some mechanics.<br /> <br /> The game also, in different places, says that armor provides Agg soak equal to Lethal soak while all the character write ups suggest that worn armor does not provide Agg soak which further supported by the fact that are rules for allowing worn armor to provide Agg soak even when it doesn't normally.<br /> <br /> My group has something we say when we run across these pieces of....frustration:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Damn it, Scion!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, if it were really left over from Aberrant, it would require a definite Epic Dexterity rating to either dodge (one dot) or pluck out of the air (four dots) bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T21:05:22-08:00","id":313474,"title":"","content":"I believe it is, instead, left over from Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T03:18:56-08:00","id":313593,"title":"","content":"Which is why I listed both games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:36:52-08:00","id":314768,"title":"","content":"After a certain point, I'm pretty sure bullets aren't even a concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:58:11-08:00","id":314938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=314768#post314768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a certain point, I'm pretty sure bullets aren't even a concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made some other rule changes that are now coming back to bite me:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>All attacks are Dex + Ability<ul><li>Sustaining a grapple may be Str + Brawl, but you need to get your hands on the slippery bugger first.</li> </ul></li> <li>Soak subtracts from the raw damage pool. Damage is then rolled. Not having any pool reduced below your Legend rating applies</li> <li>Extra successes from attack rolls do not add to your raw damage pool.</li> <li>You cannot dodge bullets without a stunt. This was done because... cinema really. I just could not picture characters casually ducking and weaving their way around a hail of gunfire.</li> </ol>This worked great at Hero and Demigod. Epic Dex made you hard to hit, and let you hit other people but it meant you only chipped away at their health levels. Epic Str didn't let you hit very often but when you did the other guys would start to fold quickly. Epic Sta made you much tougher, but not invincible.<br /> <br /> Now we are at God. At God, you can be extremely awesome at things including dodge bullets, and Fire Giants with laser rifles.<br /> <br /> Sounds like I need to cook up a &quot;Speed of the projectile does not prevent you from dodging&quot; Knack. Still allow dodging with a Stunt, but if a player doesn't want to sweat it then there's a Knack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3712-quantumpants","name":"QuantumPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T18:19:03-08:00","id":314982,"title":"","content":"My point is that if you're at least at demigod level, concussion driven projectiles are...quaint. At god level they aren't even a consideration. I'm seeing better than Superman here. And bullets aren't even an annoying factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:38:47-08:00","id":315020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuantumPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=314938#post314938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still allow dodging with a Stunt, but if a player doesn't want to sweat it then there's a Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be easier to encourage your players to stunt more. Everyone can have fun in their own way, including playing Scion without stunts, but in the games I play everyone is stunting all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T14:45:33-08:00","id":315696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=314768#post314768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a certain point, I'm pretty sure bullets aren't even a concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>That always depends on who is shooting at you and if you can move!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/308507-when-can-a-scion-dodge-bullets?p=308547#post308547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions can dodge bullets whenever they want. Whirlwind Shield is a terrible knack that implies rules that do not exist anywhere else.<br /> It's only useful if you don't have a single dot in Athletics, or you are a high strength character using knacks like Legendary Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's useful to use your dex to block bullets from hitting someone else. It's just cool looking to wu shu it away, but your non-bullet proof buddy will probably thank you afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 11-18-2014, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T19:36:29-08:00","id":315832,"title":"","content":"Nah, by the base rules, bullets are literally not a concern pretty early in.<br /> <br /> Whirlwind shield(by the book) only effects your own DV and cannot be used to save others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}